  "title": "UP Plays Important Role During Harvest Season",
  "summary": "Jeremy Ostransky is a fourth generation farmer in Bennington, Nebraska. When Ostransky was in high school, his grandpa gave him 15 acres to work. “I held on to the land while I studied agriculture business in college. After I graduated, I wanted to farm, but it just wasn’t going to work,” Ostransky said. “So I went and got a full-time job, and farmed after work and on the weekends.”",
